{"type": "FeatureCollection", "metadata": {"note": "The Central Pacific/Southern Pacific \"Shasta Route\": Roseville (junction on the transcontinental main line) north through Marysville, Chico, Red Bluff, Redding, Dunsmuir, and Weed, over the Siskiyou Summit to the Oregon border at Hornbrook, where it met the Oregon and California Railroad building south from Portland (see oc_railroad.geojson) -- together forming the first Sacramento/San Francisco - Portland rail connection, completed Dec 17 1887. This is the original, steeper Siskiyou Line alignment, distinct from the lower-grade Cascade Line via Klamath Falls that opened in 1926 (see southern_pacific_cascade.geojson).", "geometry_sources": ["OpenStreetMap (via Overpass API), ways tagged name=UP Valley Subdivision / UP Black Butte Subdivision / Siskiyou Subdivision, Dijkstra-traced with graph-bridging across small OSM node-continuity gaps"], "sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shasta_Route", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redding,_California (founded 1872 as a Central Pacific railhead)", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siskiyou_Line"], "line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6."}, "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Southern Pacific Railroad", "line": "Southern Pacific: Shasta Route", "id": "sp-shasta-route-roseville-redding", "color": "#C1272D", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 35, "speed_source": "estimated typical 19th-century steam-era mainline speed; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1869, "end": 1887, "headway_min": 720, "note": "The Central Pacific Railroad built the California and Oregon Railroad north from Roseville, reaching Marysville (1869), Chico (1870), and Redding (1872), where construction paused for roughly 15 years -- Redding was founded that year specifically as the railhead, named for CP land agent B.B. Redding. Regular passenger service ran on this completed stretch throughout the pause. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shasta_Route", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redding", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siskiyou_Line"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-121.6198645, 39.1647619], "to": [-121.819902, 39.6986385], "chord_mi": 38.39, "traced_mi": 38.42, "snap_m": [0, 0], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["UP Valley Subdivision (38.42 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-121.9562362, 39.7790118], "to": [-122.0472358, 39.9179549], "chord_mi": 10.75, "traced_mi": 10.75, "snap_m": [0, 0], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["UP Valley Subdivision (10.75 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-121.6198645, 39.1647619], "to": [-121.819902, 39.6986385], "chord_mi": 38.39, "traced_mi": 38.42, "snap_m": [0, 0], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["UP Valley Subdivision (38.42 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-121.9562362, 39.7790118], "to": [-122.0472358, 39.9179549], "chord_mi": 10.75, "traced_mi": 10.75, "snap_m": [0, 0], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["UP Valley Subdivision (10.75 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, 